**Not implemented / simplified from the spec or the arcade original:**

- **Entry-path variety:** enemies use three generic Bézier routines (top loop, side arc, chal loop) rather than the arcade's unique per-group choreography; group order (bosses first, then Goei, then Zako) is an approximation of the arcade order.
- **Escort behaviour:** escorts fly in fixed V offsets and convert to free divers when the Boss turns back or dies; the arcade's tighter escort curves are approximated.
- **Hostile captured fighter:** it turns hostile and dives/shoots, but returns to a fixed pseudo-slot at the top rather than cruising freely like the arcade.
- **Boss first hit while rammed:** a ram with a full-health Boss only costs it 1 HP (arcade behaviour) — noted since the spec says the rammed enemy "is also destroyed"; full-health bosses survive the ram.
- **Diving while player is being pulled into the beam:** other enemies keep moving (only dives/fires are suppressed during READY, as specified).
- No attract-mode demo gameplay (title screen only), no coin/credit UI, and the "1UP" player-2 area is omitted.
